0329 | \begin{remark}
0330 |     Notice that the cone of a $k$ dimensional subspace $W$ depends only on $(b_1,\ldots,b_{2k+1})$. Therefore when working on a fixed dimension $k$, we may consider cones with respect to any set of $2k+1$ linearly independent vectors.
