0372 | Before we show this implies the vanishing of all homology groups except the middle one, we need a few observations on the symmetry of $Gr(V)$. Equip $C^k(X)$ with a bilinear form:
0373 | 
0374 | \[ \langle \alpha , \beta \rangle := \sum_{W, dim(W)=k} \alpha(W)\beta(W) \]
0375 | 
